      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There was performed the analysis of the state of health of the population residing near fuel and energy complex of the Republic of Kazakhstan in the vicinity of the fuel and energy complex of Kazakhstan, namely, of the Lebyazhinsky district of the Pavlodar region. The chemicals contained in the emissions of existing enterprises of the fuel and energy complex, have a direct impact on public health. There is noted an increase of some diseases such as respiratory diseases, complications of pregnancy, childbirths and the postpartum period, diseases of the nervous system, mental and behavioral disorders, neoplasms. The child population is particularly prone to the impact of air pollutants. In children from the studied area every year the incidence of asthma is increasing by 3 times, the incidence of neoplasms--by 2 times."},
